As we discuss in our [2024 PoPETS paper](), Mastodon and federated social networking platforms present a unique perspective (and perhaps even a pivot) in the relationship between social networking websites and users, versus traditional centralized social media websites, due to the fact that Fediverse administrators often wear multiple hats when operating these websites. The legal landscape for independently operated fora is changing. While I doubt regulations will deter open-source tech enthusiasts, the new wave of administrators who have begun running e.g., Mastodon, may have apprehensions about how to move forward 



